<td><div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="description en" style="display:inline;">Attribution information, such as the author's name, e-mail, website, or signature, that was once visible in the image itself has been <b>moved into the image metadata and/or image description page</b>. This makes the image easier to reuse and more language-neutral, and makes the text easier to process and search for. Commons <a href="//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Commons:EXIF#Purpose_for_using_Exif_at_Commons" class="mw-redirect" title="Commons:EXIF">discourages</a> placing visible author information in images.</div>
<hr style="width:95%; margin:0.5em auto;">
